\subsection{Closing-interval standardization}
\label{sec:rh_close_scale}
The closing-interval model of Section~\ref{sec:rh_econ_last30} standardizes the averages of series values on its
own window $\mathcal{W}_t$ (Section~\ref{sec:rh_exp_schemes}). Rows $t'$ are trading days ($i = c$ suppressed):
\[
  z^{(k)}_{t} = \frac{\bar u^{(k)}_{t} - \operatorname{med}_{t' \in \mathcal{W}_t} \bar u^{(k)}_{t'}}
    {\max\bigl\{\mathrm{IQR}^{(k)}_{t},\ 0.01 \max_{t' \le t} \mathrm{IQR}^{(k)}_{t'},\
      \mathrm{IQR}^{\ast(k)}_{t}\bigr\}},
  \qquad \mathrm{IQR}^{(k)}_{t} = \mathrm{IQR}\bigl\{\bar u^{(k)}_{t'} : t' \in \mathcal{W}_t\bigr\}.
\]
\begin{itemize}
\item $\mathrm{IQR}^{\ast(k)}_{t}$: IQR of $\bar u^{(k)}_{t'}$, $t' < t$, over rows whose $k$-interval averaging
  window is fully observed.
\item Column whose mode accounts for at least 20\% of rows: $\mathrm{IQR}^{\ast(k)}_{t}$ also excludes rows at
  the mode.
\item $\mathrm{IQR}^{\ast(k)}_{t} = 1$ until 8 such rows exist.
\item $\bar a^{(k)}$, $\bar\chi^{(k)}$: not standardized. HAR components, calendar dummies:
  $\mathrm{IQR}^{\ast(k)}_{t} = 0$.
\item $t < W$: the first window's statistics.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Training on the last 30 minutes}
\label{sec:rh_econ_last30}
\label{sec:rh_results_pooled}
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Closing-interval estimation scheme ($\mathcal I = \{c\}$).} As a final refinement, we restrict estimation of each model class in Section~\ref{sec:rh_methods_models} exclusively to observations from the closing half hour $i = c$ (15:30--16:00 ET), matching the estimation domain of the daily HAR benchmark.
  \begin{itemize}
  \item Under this scheme, each trading day contributes a single observation, so a period corresponds to one trading day and the rolling window $\mathcal W_t = \{t - W, \dots, t - 1\}$ spans $W = \cmPtFitWin$ trading days (Appendix~\ref{sec:rh_exp_schemes}). Rolling standardization of the exogenous series averages on $\mathcal W_t$ follows Appendix~\ref{sec:rh_close_scale}.
  \item We hold the predictor sets, evaluation sample $\mathcal T_{\mathrm{oos}}$, and straddle trading rules unchanged; statistical accuracy is reported in Table~\ref{tab:rh_oos_last30} over the same forecast origins as Table~\ref{tab:rh_oos}.
    % 2026-10-15 (user): Table 1 split; was "accuracy in Table~\ref{tab:rh_oos}, columns ``Last 30 minutes''."
  \end{itemize}
\item \textbf{Improvements in QLIKE accuracy.} Training solely on the closing interval reduces mean QLIKE relative to pooled intraday training in every model class and under both predictor sets. Specifically, the percentage excess loss of the pooled intraday forecast $f_{m,\mathcal X,\{1,\dots,M\}}$ relative to the closing-interval forecast $f_{m,\mathcal X,\{c\}}$, $\Delta\% = 100\bigl(\bar L^{\mathrm{pool}}/\bar L^{\mathrm{close}} - 1\bigr)$, is strictly positive throughout:
  \begin{itemize}
  \item for penalized linear models, pooling increases mean QLIKE by $+\rhrLinBasePoolPctMin\%$ to $+\rhrLinBasePoolPctMax\%$ on the HAR benchmark ($\DM$ from \rhrLinBasePoolDmMin{} to \rhrLinBasePoolDmMax, all significant at the 5\% level) and by $+\rhrLinAllPoolPctMin\%$ to $+\rhrLinAllPoolPctMax\%$ on the full predictor set (significant for the lasso);
